{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC -> TEST MAP (the discipline added after f184 closed late with half a criterion untested). tests/unit/test_openai_compatible_provider.py, 11 tests: AC1 documented recipe end-to-end => test_documented_local_server_recipe_returns_a_structured_verdict; AC2 base_url must not hijack selection => test_base_url_does_not_hijack_provider_selection; AC3a refusal gone => test_check_config_accepts_a_valid_base_url; AC3b api_key without base_url => test_api_key_without_base_url_is_a_config_error; AC3c non-absolute base_url => test_non_absolute_base_url_is_a_config_error; AC3d missing extra names install cmd => test_missing_openai_extra_raises_naming_the_install_command; AC4 ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL gateway pin => test_non_loopback_anthropic_base_url_is_respected_as_a_gateway; AC5 override applied => test_custom_endpoint_withdraws_native_structured_output; AC6 override surgical => test_profile_override_is_surgical; AC7 bare openai builds no provider => test_bare_openai_string_without_base_url_builds_no_provider; plus contrast case test_native_output_still_selected_for_a_hosted_openai_model (the withdrawal must not leak to the hosted API). AC8 (providers.py<300 LOC, no openai branch in runner.py), AC9 (agents extra unchanged) and AC10 (lint/typecheck/full make test) are verified by grep/wc/CI rather than unit tests. MECHANISM CORRECTION recorded in the plan: the profile override rides the PROVIDER (a rebar OpenAIProvider subclass overriding the model_profile staticmethod), NOT OpenAIChatModel(profile=...) — because rebars S1 seam returns a Provider and infer_model builds the model itself, so a model-level argument is unreachable from the seam. pydantic-ai resolves profile=profile or provider.model_profile; verified end-to-end that the subclass yields model.profile.supports_json_schema_output False while supports_tools stays True, surviving the OpenAIModelProfile.update() applied afterwards. RED evidence: 6 failed for the right reasons (2x the actual loud refusal LLMConfigError does-not-yet-support, 2x assert True is False for the missing override, 1x wrong error text, 1x DID NOT RAISE), 5 passing are regression guards that must STAY passing."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785379752993574001,"uuid":"8ec5d68d-97fa-4fba-8076-41a032357e92"}